{"sections":[{"title":"Create your first 2D scene","estimatedTimeInMinutes":20,"kind":"hero","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.2 or later","chapter":"Create your first 2D game project.","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to create your first 2D scene using AdaEngine.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"anchor":"Intro","stepsSection":[],"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","media":"CF2G-3-5.mov","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the first 2D scene, we will try to repeat this example. We’ll look at adding a scene and a camera."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In addition, we’ll learn how to add sprites and movement systems."}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"title":"Intro"},{"anchor":"Create-an-app","stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null,"code":"CF2G-1-1-app.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the previous tutorial, we’ve created an app and an empty window scene."}]}],"type":"step"},{"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null,"code":"CF2G-1-2-scene.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Let’s create the game logic. To do this, let’s create a file named "},{"code":"FirstScene.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and import AdaEngine."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"After that, create a struct named "},{"code":"FirstScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that conforms to "},{"code":"Plugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a method named "},{"code":"setup(in app: AppWorlds)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" where we will set up entities in our game world."}]}],"type":"step"},{"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null,"code":"CF2G-1-4-app.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now add the "},{"code":"FirstScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin to the app using the "},{"code":"addPlugins","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}]}],"type":"step"}],"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First, we need to create base files to launch our application."}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"title":"Create an app"},{"anchor":"Create-a-main-camera","stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"CF2G-2-1-camera.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Let’s create our 2D camera. Spawn an entity with the "},{"code":"Camera2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle."}]}]},{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"CF2G-2-2-camera.swift","runtimePreview":"CF2G-2-1.png","type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let’s fill the camera background with a sky blue color."}]}]}],"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AdaEngine uses the Entity Component System paradigm where all game objects are called "},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Entities are objects that store user or engine data like position, scale, mesh instance, audio, etc. This data is called components, and they should conform to the "},{"code":"Component","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"By default, "},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is an empty object without any components."}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Camera","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a component that determines where all entities will be rendered. AdaEngine supports rendering to a texture or to the "},{"code":"Window","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". We recommend using engine component bundles like "},{"code":"Camera2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Camera3D","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because the engine provides additional components for rendering and audio capabilities."}]}],"kind":"fullWidth"}],"title":"Create a main camera."},{"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now we can create our first custom sprite."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"title":"First sprite","anchor":"First-sprite","stepsSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First, we should create an assets folder where we will store our game assets, like sprite sheets, sounds, shaders, etc. Let’s create a folder named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Assets"},{"type":"text","text":" and add any sprite sheets you want. We will use this sprite sheet:"}]}],"code":null,"type":"step","caption":[],"media":"CF2G-3-1.png","runtimePreview":null},{"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can download this texture by right-clicking on the image and saving it to the downloads folder."}]}],"media":"CF2G-3-2.png","code":null,"runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the end, we should have this file structure in our project. AdaEngine doesn’t use xcassets."}]}]},{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"CF2G-3-1-sprite.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawn a player entity in the game world. The player entity will store our sprite component and other player data in the future."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Let’s create an image from a file using a special resource manager object. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetsManager"},{"type":"text","text":" manages and caches game and engine resources. In our case, we should load an image from a file named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"characters_packed.png"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.main"},{"text":" as a search path.","type":"text"}]}],"code":"CF2G-3-2-sprite.swift","type":"step","caption":[],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null},{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"CF2G-3-3-sprite.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To split the sprite sheet image into sprites, we can use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TextureAtlas"},{"type":"text","text":" object. This object takes an image, sprite size, and margin between sprites if needed. In our case, we have a margin between sprites of 4px horizontally and 1px vertically, and a sprite size of 20px width and 23px height."}]}]},{"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a new sprite component to the entity in the "},{"code":"spawn","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method. As you can see, we use subscripts in our "},{"code":"TextureAtlas","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance where 7 is the column number in our sprite sheet and 1 is the row number."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"CF2G-3-3.png","media":null,"code":"CF2G-3-4-sprite.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now we can add our sprite to the player entity using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sprite","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" component. This component is efficient for rendering because it uses a special batching system and requires fewer drawing calls.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step"},{"caption":[],"runtimePreview":"CF2G-3-4.png","media":null,"code":"CF2G-3-5-sprite.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"And finally, let’s add a special "},{"code":"Transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" component that describes the position of our entity on the screen."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step"}]},{"contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"We did a lot of work, but our scene looks very simple. We should add more life to our player entity. All game logic is described in special objects named ","type":"text"},{"code":"System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A system is a unit that executes each game loop and manipulates entities and their data. We will use one to add life to our player.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"title":"Make it move","anchor":"Make-it-move","stepsSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"First, we should create a special tag component named ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlayerComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". We will use this component in the near future; it indicates that this entity is a player.","type":"text"}]}],"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"CF2G-4-1-player.swift","type":"step","runtimePreview":null},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create a new function named ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlayerMovement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and annotate this function with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro. This system will listen to user inputs and move our player component on the screen.","type":"text"}]}],"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"CF2G-4-2-player.swift","type":"step","runtimePreview":null},{"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null,"code":"CF2G-4-3-player.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the new system to our game scene. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro will create a new system with the same name as the function with the suffix ","type":"text"},{"code":"System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Our system will be initialized once on app launch.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step"},{"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null,"code":"CF2G-4-4-player.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlayerMovementSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", add a new function parameter named ","type":"text"},{"code":"playerTransform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FilterQuery<Ref<Transform>, With<PlayerComponent>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This object will query the world and return components that conform to your predicate. In our case, we require one mutable component ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a filter that indicates we need entities with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlayerComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step"},{"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null,"code":"CF2G-4-5-player.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a new function parameter named ","type":"text"},{"code":"speed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Local<Float>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type. This is a special type that stores a value available only within the system.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now we can update our player position. AdaEngine can handle keyboard inputs for us. We should listen to keyboard inputs, and if a key is pressed, we should change the player transform."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Using the special ","type":"text"},{"code":"Input","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object, we can check if a key is pressed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Add an ","type":"text"},{"code":"if","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" condition where we will listen to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"w","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" key. If the key is pressed, add the speed multiplied by delta time. We do this for a smooth transition between frames.","type":"text"}]}],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null,"code":"CF2G-4-6-player.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Let’s add a new function parameter named ","type":"text"},{"code":"deltaTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Res<DeltaTime>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type and ","type":"text"},{"code":"input","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Res<Input>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". These are queries to resources in the world.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step"},{"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Run the app and try to move your player.","type":"text"}]}],"runtimePreview":"CF2G-3-5.mov","media":null,"code":"CF2G-4-7-player.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Finally, add the same logic for other keys — ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"s","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"d","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step"}]}]},{"title":"Player and Text in Ada Engine","kind":"callToAction","action":{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Get started","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}]},"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to add a player component that you can control and how to add text and various labels to your game scene."}]}],"kind":"project","hierarchy":{"modules":[{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateProject","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateProject#Create-project-using-Xcode","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Intro","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-an-app","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-a-main-camera","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#First-sprite","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Make-it-move","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Player-component","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Text-component","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Base-of-Event-Subscriber-pattern","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Subscribe-to-scene-events","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Type-of-events","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Additional-for-physics","kind":"task"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/Create-your-first-2D-game-project."},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Create-the-app-shell","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Layout-with-stacks","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Add-a-button-and-state","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Debug-overlays","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Create-the-view","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Prepare-layout-helpers","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Create-a-custom-TextRenderer","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Apply-and-animate","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Set-up-the-world","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Create-the-input-system","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Read-buttons","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Move-and-rumble","kind":"task"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UI-and-Input"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine","paths":[["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/$volume","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/Create-your-first-2D-game-project."]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/tutorials\/adaengine\/createfirst2dscene"]}],"metadata":{"categoryPathComponent":"AdaEngine","role":"project","title":"Create your first 2D scene","category":"Ada Engine"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/UIBasics":{"estimatedTime":"15min","role":"project","kind":"project","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a simple UI screen using AdaEngine views. You will create a window, layout a few elements, and add a button with state."}],"title":"UI Basics","type":"topic","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/uibasics"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/PlayerAndText#Add-Text-component":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Text-component","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to add a player component that you can control and how to add text and various labels to your game scene."}],"title":"Add Text component","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/playerandtext#Add-Text-component"},"CF2G-4-6-player.swift":{"syntax":"swift","content":["import AdaEngine","","struct FirstScene: Plugin {","    func setup(in app: AppWorlds) {","        \/** Collapsed code *\/","    }","}","","@Component","struct PlayerComponent {}","","@System","func PlayerMovement(","    _ playerTransform: FIlterQuery<Ref<Transform>, With<PlayerComponent>>,","    _ speed: Local<Float> = 3.0,","    _ deltaTime: Res<DeltaTime>,","    _ input: Res<Input>",") {","    playerTransform.forEach { transform in","        if input.wrappedValue.isKeyPressed(.w) {","            transform.position.y += speed.wrappedValue * deltaTime.wrappedValue.deltaTime","        }","    }","}"],"identifier":"CF2G-4-6-player.swift","type":"file","fileName":"FirstScene.swift","fileType":"swift","highlights":[{"line":15},{"line":16},{"line":17},{"line":19},{"line":20},{"line":21},{"line":22},{"line":23}]},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/GamepadInput#Read-buttons":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Read-buttons","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a small scene that spawns a player entity and moves it with a gamepad."}],"title":"Read buttons","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/gamepadinput#Read-buttons"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/GamepadInput#Set-up-the-world":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Set-up-the-world","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a small scene that spawns a player entity and moves it with a gamepad."}],"title":"Set up the world","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/gamepadinput#Set-up-the-world"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/PlayerAndText#Add-Player-component":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Player-component","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to add a player component that you can control and how to add text and various labels to your game scene."}],"title":"Add Player component","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/playerandtext#Add-Player-component"},"CF2G-4-7-player.swift":{"syntax":"swift","content":["import AdaEngine","","struct FirstScene: Plugin {","    func setup(in app: AppWorlds) {","        \/** Collapsed code *\/","    }","}","","@Component","struct PlayerComponent {}","","@System","func PlayerMovement(","    _ playerTransform: FIlterQuery<Ref<Transform>, With<PlayerComponent>>,","    _ speed: Local<Float> = 3.0,","    _ deltaTime: Res<DeltaTime>,","    _ input: Res<Input>",") {","    playerTransform.forEach { transform in","        if input.wrappedValue.isKeyPressed(.w) {","            transform.position.y += speed.wrappedValue * deltaTime.wrappedValue.deltaTime","        }","","        if input.wrappedValue.isKeyPressed(.s) {","            transform.position.y -= speed.wrappedValue * deltaTime.wrappedValue.deltaTime","        }","","        if input.wrappedValue.isKeyPressed(.a) {","            transform.position.x -= speed.wrappedValue * deltaTime.wrappedValue.deltaTime","        }","","        if input.wrappedValue.isKeyPressed(.d) {","            transform.position.x += speed.wrappedValue * deltaTime.wrappedValue.deltaTime","        }","    }","}"],"identifier":"CF2G-4-7-player.swift","type":"file","fileName":"FirstScene.swift","fileType":"swift","highlights":[{"line":23},{"line":24},{"line":25},{"line":26},{"line":27},{"line":28},{"line":29},{"line":30},{"line":31},{"line":32},{"line":33},{"line":34}]},"CF2G-3-3.png":{"alt":"Our sprite sheet","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/AdaEngine\/CF2G-3-3.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"type":"image","identifier":"CF2G-3-3.png"},"doc://AdaEngine/tutorials/AdaEngine/CreateFirst2DScene#Intro":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Intro","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to create your first 2D scene using AdaEngine."}],"title":"Intro","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/adaengine\/createfirst2dscene#Intro"},"CF2G-2-1-camera.swift":{"content":["import AdaEngine","","struct FirstScene: Plugin {","    func setup(in app: AppWorlds) {","        app.spawn(bundle: Camera2D())","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","highlights":[],"identifier":"CF2G-2-1-camera.swift","fileType":"swift","type":"file","fileName":"FirstScene.swift"},"CF2G-3-1-sprite.swift":{"syntax":"swift","identifier":"CF2G-3-1-sprite.swift","content":["import AdaEngine","","struct FirstScene: Plugin {","    func setup(in app: AppWorlds) {","        let camera = Camera()","        camera.backgroundColor = Color(45\/255, 171\/255, 255\/255, 1)","        app.spawn(bundle: Camera2D(camera: camera))","","        app.spawn(\"Player\")","    }","}"],"type":"file","fileName":"FirstScene.swift","fileType":"swift","highlights":[]},"CF2G-4-1-player.swift":{"syntax":"swift","identifier":"CF2G-4-1-player.swift","content":["import AdaEngine","","struct FirstScene: Plugin {","    func setup(in app: AppWorlds) {","        let camera = Camera()","        camera.backgroundColor = Color(45\/255, 171\/255, 255\/255, 1)","        app.spawn(bundle: Camera2D(camera: camera))","","        let spriteSheetImage = try! AssetsManager.loadSync(Image.self, at: \"@res:\/\/characters_packed.png\").asset!","        let spriteSheet = TextureAtlas(from: spriteSheetImage, size: [20, 23], margin: [4, 1])","","        app.spawn(\"Player\") {","    